 "Each vintage era has its own signature. The 70s are warm, with yellow highlights and brown shadows, great for late sun and wooden cafés. The 80s are faded and low in saturation, with shadows that never go fully black, suiting sky and sea shots. The 90s are the compact flash camera: punchy colour, high contrast, often an orange date stamp in the corner, ideal at night and with friends.": 1,
