 "At what temperature should kids stay inside?": 1,
 "There is no single cut-off, but when the feels-like temperature passes about 35°C or UV reaches 8 or more, avoid midday outdoor play and move it to early morning or late afternoon, in shade with plenty of water.": 1,
 "Do kids need sunscreen on cloudy days?": 1,
 "Yes. UV passes through cloud, so go by the UV index rather than whether it looks sunny. For babies under six months, prefer shade and covering clothing and ask a doctor before using sunscreen.": 1,
